    <item>
      <title>Anion manipulation for breaking through 3.0 V of aluminium–graphite batteries</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79156-7</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 13 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79156-7"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-79156-7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Aluminium–graphite batteries are limited by electrolyte decomposition above 2.5 V. Here, authors regulate chloroaluminate anions with a fluorine-rich, framework-confined quasi-solid-state electrolyte, enabling stable 3.0 V operation for Al | |Graphite cells.</content:encoded>
      <dc:title>Anion manipulation for breaking through 3.0 V of aluminium–graphite batteries</dc:title>
