      <title>Thin-film lithium niobate waveguide-integrated p-i-n Tungsten selenide photodiodes with 10Gbit/s data reception</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79595-2</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 12 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-79595-2"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-79595-2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Thin-film lithium niobate (TFLN) is a promising photonic platform, but its integration with 2D materials remains challenging. Here, the authors report the realization of TFLN-based waveguide-integrated WSe2 photodetectors, showing a 3-dB bandwidth up to 1.12 GHz, up to 10 Gbit/s data rates and responsivity up to 492 mA/W in the visible range.</content:encoded>
